      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your sense of feeling lost and overwhelmed at the thought of moving forward is completely understandable. It's normal to grieve the loss of purpose after so many years of meaningful work. Perhaps we could explore other options together that might reignite a spark or assist in adjusting to this new chapter of your life. Engaging with your surroundings or connecting with people who appreciate your history as a surgeon could help bridge the gap between past and present. It may also help to volunteer at a level that doesn't require your surgical expertise if that's something you're considering. When you're ready, we can seek out communities or organizations that value the skills and experiences you've accumulated. Your life story matters just as much now as it did on the operating table.",
